<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Naimbana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1793</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as King Naimbana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Naimbana was king of Koya, a Temne state on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sierra-leone">Sierra Leone</a> estuary, in the late 18th century. In 1788 he confirmed the grant of land on the peninsula made by his subordinate <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-tom-koya">King Tom</a> to British abolitionists for the Province of Freedom, the origin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freetown">Freetown</a>. He sent his son John Frederic to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> to be educated; the young man died on the voyage home in 1793.</p></div>
